---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ScreenshotSlot from '../components/ScreenshotSlot.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — TokGrid';
const description =
  'How TokGrid handles public page data, extension storage, subscription validation, feedback forms, and this static website.';
const gaEnabled = Boolean(SITE.gaMeasurementId);
const lastUpdated = 'November 8, 2026';
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="container-page py-10 sm:py-14">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
          { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-600">
          Legal & privacy
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
          This policy describes the TokGrid Chrome extension and this website. It is
          written to match how the current build behaves, including the parts it does{' '}
          <strong>not</strong> do.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
      <div class="not-prose mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/70 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-brand-950">
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <Icon name="shield" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-brand-700" />
          <p>
            <strong>Short version:</strong> the extension processes public page data in
            your browser. Page data is not uploaded to TokGrid. A separate license check
            may contact the subscription server with an account identifier and token.
            This website is static; analytics is described in section 7.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers the TokGrid browser extension and the public website at{' '}
        <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a>. It does not cover TikTok, the Chrome Web
        Store, Tally, the payment processor, or any other third-party service you choose
        to use. Those services have their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What the extension reads</h2>
      <p>
        TokGrid is built for public TikTok pages you have opened. It reads information
        that is already present in the page: cards rendered in the DOM, read-only React
        props exposed by the page, and embedded page JSON. The fields can include video
        IDs, descriptions, counts, author details, product anchors, video qualities, and
        subtitle links, depending on what the page makes available.
      </p>
      <p>
        The extension does not bypass login, CAPTCHA, or rate limits. It is intended for
        public, logged-out pages. It does not collect private messages, account
        credentials, or content that is not already loaded in the page.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Where page data is processed</h2>
      <p>
        Page data is processed locally in your browser. TokGrid does not upload page data
        to a TokGrid server. It does not overwrite <code>fetch</code> or{' '}
        <code>XMLHttpRequest</code>, does not intercept network requests, and does not
        make background TikTok API calls to collect data. There is no analytics or
        telemetry in the extension.
      </p>
      <p>
        Settings and an encrypted subscription credential are stored in{' '}
        <code>chrome.storage.local</code>. Page content used by the panel is kept in the
        page context and is not sent to TokGrid.
      </p>

      <h2>4. What leaves the browser</h2>
      <p>
        Three narrow flows can involve a network request. They are separate from page
        data collection:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Downloads and subtitles.</strong> When you click a download control,
          the extension requests the media or subtitle URL from TikTok media domains and
          writes the file locally. The request is user-initiated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Subscription validation.</strong> When you open the subscription flow,
          restore a token, refresh status, return from checkout, reopen the extension with
          a pending payment, or trigger a paid feature while a check is required, the
          extension contacts the license server at <code>pandahi.cc</code>. The request
          can include an account identifier, token, channel, and operation type. It does{' '}
          <strong>not</strong> include page data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Feedback forms.</strong> The Feedback tab opens a Tally-hosted form in a
          new page. The URL can be prefilled with a device ID, extension version, and
          interface language. The form content (email, review link, or message) is
          submitted by you on Tally’s page. The extension does not read, save, or upload
          those form contents and does not receive a host permission for Tally.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Permissions</h2>
      <p>The current extension manifest requests:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>storage</code> — settings and the encrypted subscription credential.</li>
        <li>
          Host permissions for <code>*.tiktok.com</code>, <code>*.tiktokcdn.com</code>,
          and <code>*.tiktokv.com</code> — the read-only page script and user-initiated
          media/subtitle requests.
        </li>
        <li>
          Host permission for <code>pandahi.cc</code> — subscription activation, token
          restore, status refresh, return from checkout, and the pending-payment check.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The extension does not request <code>downloads</code>, <code>webRequest</code>,
        <code>scripting</code>, <code>tabs</code>, or <code>&lt;all_urls&gt;</code>.
        Single-file downloads use a local Blob and a download link. Batch downloads use
        the browser’s File System Access API and a folder you explicitly choose.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Storage and retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Settings stay in local extension storage until you clear them or uninstall the extension.</li>
        <li>The encrypted subscription credential stays until you sign out, clear it, or uninstall.</li>
        <li>The extension’s network activity log is kept in memory and is cleared when the page is refreshed.</li>
        <li>Downloaded files are written to the folder you choose and remain under your control.</li>
        <li>Tally submissions are handled by the operator for support and reward follow-up, subject to the form’s own terms.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="not-prose my-10">
        <ScreenshotSlot
          id="privacy"
          caption="The Settings and privacy center referenced in this policy."
        />
      </div>

      <h2>7. This website</h2>
      <p>
        This website is a static site. It does not load a tag manager, advertising
        pixels, embedded videos, third-party fonts, or contact forms. It does not set
        its own cookies. When Google Analytics is enabled for the build (see below),
        GA may set its own cookies. The site is designed to be served by a static hosting
        provider, such as Cloudflare Pages; the hosting provider may process standard
        request metadata (such as IP address, user agent, and timestamp) for delivery,
        security, and abuse prevention under its own policy.
      </p>

      {
        gaEnabled ? (
          <>
            <h3>Google Analytics (enabled on this build)</h3>
            <p>
              This build uses Google Analytics 4 with measurement ID
              <code>{SITE.gaMeasurementId}</code>. GA4 may collect page views,
              approximate location derived from the request, device/browser information,
              and interaction events, and may set <code>_ga</code> cookies. TokGrid uses
              this only to understand aggregate website usage. You can block GA with
              browser settings, an extension, or a consent control where one is required.
              The extension itself does not contain Google Analytics.
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h3>Google Analytics (not enabled on this build)</h3>
            <p>
              No Google Analytics measurement ID is configured for this build, so the
              GA tag is not rendered. If a measurement ID is later configured at build
              time, this section and the site’s script loading will change together.
            </p>
          </>
        )
      }

      <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set its own cookies. If Google Analytics is enabled in
        this build, GA may set its own cookies as described above. The extension uses
        extension storage, not website cookies, for its settings.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Third parties</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Chrome Web Store</strong> — distribution and installation. Its own policies apply.</li>
        <li><strong>pandahi.cc</strong> — subscription checkout and license validation.</li>
        <li><strong>Tally</strong> — user-opened feedback and reward forms.</li>
        <li><strong>Static hosting provider</strong> — website delivery and standard request logs.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — when enabled for the site build.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        TokGrid does not sell page data. It does not use page data for advertising. It
        does not share page data with the subscription server.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Clear settings and page data from the extension’s Settings tab.</li>
        <li>Uninstall the extension to remove its local extension storage.</li>
        <li>Refresh the page to clear the in-memory activity log.</li>
        <li>Choose your own download folder, or cancel a batch before or during a run.</li>
        <li>Block or delete analytics cookies in your browser if GA is enabled.</li>
        <li>Contact support to request help with a Tally submission or a privacy question.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or support, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`} class="font-semibold">
          {SITE.supportEmail}
        </a>
        . Do not send page data, account credentials, or subscription tokens in a support
        request.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may change as the extension and website evolve. The “Last updated”
        date at the top will change when it does. Material changes should be reviewed
        before the next public release.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
        <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Independent product</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          TokGrid is an independent browser extension and is not affiliated with,
          endorsed by, or sponsored by TikTok or ByteDance. TikTok and related marks are
          trademarks of their respective owners.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
